It wasn't just there.

01:21:42.980 --> 01:21:43.820
So I'm not crazy.

01:21:43.820 --> 01:21:45.740
You're not crazy, she's right.

01:21:45.740 --> 01:21:48.100
For me, so we had an issue recently

01:21:48.100 --> 01:21:49.980
where a client sent me an upset email

01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:50.820
and he was like,

01:21:50.820 --> 01:21:54.300
I was getting 28 cases and I got 17 this month.

01:21:54.340 --> 01:21:55.180
What went wrong?

01:21:55.180 --> 01:21:57.500
And like, of course I just go to data, right?

01:21:57.500 --> 01:21:58.900
And I go and I look at results.

01:21:58.900 --> 01:22:00.300
Has anything changed in results?

01:22:00.300 --> 01:22:01.820
Then I went and I looked at call volume.

01:22:01.820 --> 01:22:03.420
Call volume was up.

01:22:03.420 --> 01:22:05.540
So I called his cell phone.

01:22:05.540 --> 01:22:06.660
I thought I was calling his cell phone,

01:22:06.660 --> 01:22:08.140
but I had just upgraded cell phones

01:22:08.140 --> 01:22:10.220
and it actually went to the firm.

01:22:10.220 --> 01:22:13.580
And it took seven rings for the firm to pick up.

01:22:13.580 --> 01:22:14.420
I called him back.

01:22:14.420 --> 01:22:15.260
I told him what happened.

01:22:15.260 --> 01:22:16.100
He fixed it.

01:22:16.100 --> 01:22:18.300
The next month they got 34 cases.

01:22:18.300 --> 01:22:19.140
Wow.

01:22:19.140 --> 01:22:20.860
So I know, but it's just,

01:22:20.860 --> 01:22:23.180
for me, it's hard to get everyone on board

01:22:23.220 --> 01:22:26.260
with this, you know, belief, right?

01:22:26.260 --> 01:22:27.940
Like everybody just talks about like,

01:22:27.940 --> 01:22:30.140
